main.py
--unwind 5

^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Unannotated empty dict with int-key subscript-assigns: the first
d[k] = v rebuilds the dict with the actual key/value element types so
distinct int keys aren't lossily coerced to the default str key type.
(Building such a dict incrementally inside a loop still requires an
explicit `d: dict[int, int] = {}` annotation — the rebuild only fires
outside loops.)
